config ZMK_BATTERY_LOG
    bool "Periodically log split peripheral battery levels"
    depends on ZMK_SPLIT_BLE_CENTRAL_BATTERY_LEVEL_FETCHING
    help
      ZMK exposes peripheral battery levels only over BLE (the BAS proxy
      service). A dongle attached to the host over USB HID has no way to
      report them, so this prints them to the console instead - pair it with
      the zmk-usb-logging snippet and the levels come out of a CDC ACM port
      the host can read.

config ZMK_BATTERY_LOG_INTERVAL_S
    int "Seconds between battery log lines"
    default 10
    depends on ZMK_BATTERY_LOG

config ZMK_BATTERY_LOG_LABELS
    string "Comma-separated name per peripheral slot"
    default "left,right"
    depends on ZMK_BATTERY_LOG
    help
      Peripheral slots are handed out in connection/bond order and the central
      never learns which half is which, so the mapping is a local fact, not
      something the firmware can discover. Slots past the end of this list are
      logged by number. Verify with: power one half off and watch the log for
      "Releasing peripheral slot at <n>".
